(The talk of the town last week)

3
00:00:06,663 --> 00:00:08,563
(Moo chewy cookies)

4
00:00:08,663 --> 00:00:09,932
("Jun Hyun Moo's Moo Chewy Cookies Tops the Ratings")

5
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:11,203
("Moo Chewy Cookies Taste as Shocking as They Look")

6
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:13,072
(To stabilize the supply of DCC,)

7
00:00:13,097 --> 00:00:14,597
(Moomoo was deployed.)

8
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:16,903
(Let's start from scratch.)

9
00:00:17,203 --> 00:00:18,973
(From shelling pistachios...)

10
00:00:19,213 --> 00:00:20,943
(to making his own kadayif,)

11
00:00:21,173 --> 00:00:22,713
(he made Moo chewy cookies from scratch.)

12
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:26,682
(I screamed when I saw the pistachios fall.)

13
00:00:26,683 --> 00:00:27,813
(Come on, you've got to be kidding me. It's so stressful.)

14
00:00:28,923 --> 00:00:30,623
(Getting a headache)

15
00:00:31,123 --> 00:00:33,693
(I decided to make DCC and ought to see it through.)

16
00:00:34,953 --> 00:00:36,893
(A huge chewy cookie)

17
00:00:37,493 --> 00:00:39,493
(Here are Dubai-style pancakes.)

18
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:42,063
(Despite how it looks, it tastes authentic.)

19
00:00:43,303 --> 00:00:45,473
(Thick and moist)

20
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:47,933
(Do you want it?)

21
00:00:48,273 --> 00:00:49,903
(After wrapping them in hip packaging, he headed...)

22
00:00:50,373 --> 00:00:52,913
(Moomoo's After-Sales Service)

23
00:00:53,343 --> 00:00:55,012
(Out of gratitude,)

24
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:58,013
(he decided to provide after-sales service.)

25
00:00:58,513 --> 00:00:59,953
(Utterly satisfied)

26
00:01:00,183 --> 00:01:01,712
(The next spot, Moomoo's dream spot)

27
00:01:01,713 --> 00:01:03,653
(Hue's house)

28
00:01:03,853 --> 00:01:04,983
(People line up to buy that.)

29
00:01:05,353 --> 00:01:06,792
(I bought it for you.)

30
00:01:06,793 --> 00:01:08,253
(That's for me?)

31
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:10,092
(He gave Hue keyboard pedals.)

32
00:01:10,093 --> 00:01:11,363
(You're like Santa Claus.)

33
00:01:11,693 --> 00:01:13,893
(I'm loving myself right now.)

34
00:01:14,293 --> 00:01:16,363
(Moo chewy cookies for the members)

35
00:01:17,003 --> 00:01:19,873
(Can you give me three more?)

36
00:01:20,303 --> 00:01:21,803
(Moo chewy cookies were a hit too.)

37
00:01:22,343 --> 00:01:23,802
(He headed to Jae Hyeon's house next.)

38
00:01:23,803 --> 00:01:24,903
(I'm here.)

39
00:01:25,613 --> 00:01:27,373
(Winking)

40
00:01:27,943 --> 00:01:30,283
(My intercom doesn't have a screen.)

41
00:01:30,483 --> 00:01:32,553
(Making a scene)

42
00:01:33,683 --> 00:01:36,353
(Hyun Moo arrives in the parking lot of Jae Hyeon's building.)

43
00:01:37,283 --> 00:01:39,893
(Struggling)

44
00:01:40,423 --> 00:01:41,453
Hyun Moo.

45
00:01:42,593 --> 00:01:45,362
(The third member shows up with a smile.)

46
00:01:45,363 --> 00:01:47,732
The third spot of Moomoo's After-Sales Service is...

47
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:50,263
the new owner of the oven, Jae Hyeon's house.

48
00:01:51,463 --> 00:01:52,832
(At the last bazaar,)

49
00:01:52,833 --> 00:01:54,473
(Hyun Moo's oven was a headache.)

50
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:57,803
(Who's going to buy that?)

51
00:01:59,013 --> 00:02:01,142
(But Jae Hyeon was the only one who showed interest.)

52
00:02:01,143 --> 00:02:03,013
(The listed price is between 3,500 to 4,500 dollars.)

53
00:02:03,583 --> 00:02:05,182
(But I'll sell it to you for 1,000 dollars.)

54
00:02:05,183 --> 00:02:07,813
(We have a deal!)

55
00:02:08,653 --> 00:02:10,922
(He gladly bought it for his friends who were planning to open a cafe.)

56
00:02:10,923 --> 00:02:13,053
(He gladly bought it for his friends who were planning to open a cafe.)

57
00:02:13,493 --> 00:02:15,762
That was the most expensive item at the bazaar that day.

58
00:02:15,763 --> 00:02:16,893
- Right. - Yes.

59
00:02:17,863 --> 00:02:19,862
(The oven will finally meet its owner.)

60
00:02:19,863 --> 00:02:21,462
I can't believe the oven got a new owner.

61
00:02:21,463 --> 00:02:22,532
- This is... - Wait.

62
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:23,833
- Hyun Moo, grab the bottom. - Wait.

63
00:02:24,203 --> 00:02:25,803
One, two, three. Just like this. We got it.

64
00:02:27,073 --> 00:02:29,302
- Do I need all of them? - They're all yours.

65
00:02:29,303 --> 00:02:31,103
- Really? - Yes. I'm giving them to you.

66
00:02:31,473 --> 00:02:32,712
- There are stones too. - Okay.

67
00:02:32,713 --> 00:02:34,673
- You need them. - When do you need them?

68
00:02:34,873 --> 00:02:36,042
For baking.

69
00:02:36,043 --> 00:02:37,542
The oven rack looks really good too.

70
00:02:37,543 --> 00:02:38,952
- It's... - He got it custom-made.

71
00:02:38,953 --> 00:02:40,213
- I did. Yes. - Really?

72
00:02:40,553 --> 00:02:42,883
Hyun Moo. Someone finally recognizes its value...

73
00:02:42,983 --> 00:02:44,423
- after it got sold. - Exactly.

74
00:02:44,553 --> 00:02:46,193
You can move another oven to his house then.

75
00:02:46,553 --> 00:02:47,753
I'll help you.

76
00:02:47,923 --> 00:02:49,192
- Do I have to be... - You must transport it.

77
00:02:49,193 --> 00:02:50,723
responsible for its final transport too?

78
00:02:51,823 --> 00:02:53,032
It's like life insurance.

79
00:02:53,033 --> 00:02:54,833
- You have to help him sell it. - I'm selling life insurance.

80
00:02:55,633 --> 00:02:56,862
- Finally. - Hyun Moo, wait.

81
00:02:56,863 --> 00:02:57,933
What?

82
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:00,173
- What? - There are stairs to the elevator.

83
00:03:00,303 --> 00:03:01,303
- What? - What?

84
00:03:01,304 --> 00:03:02,542
It doesn't directly lead to the elevator.

85
00:03:02,543 --> 00:03:03,902
No. We have to walk up the stairs.

86
00:03:03,903 --> 00:03:04,943
- Right. - That's bad.

87
00:03:07,243 --> 00:03:09,482
- Install the oven here. - No. We can get going.

88
00:03:09,483 --> 00:03:10,713
- We can do this. - Hey, this...

89
00:03:11,383 --> 00:03:13,353
- Should we push them like this? - Yes, let's go.

90
00:03:13,813 --> 00:03:16,253
But there must be only a few stairs, not that many.

91
00:03:16,583 --> 00:03:18,852
- But the oven was quite heavy. - But it was still pretty tough.

92
00:03:18,853 --> 00:03:20,293
- Just watch. - Right, the oven is really heavy.

93
00:03:21,123 --> 00:03:22,153
Hold on.

94
00:03:22,323 --> 00:03:23,662
- The door is open. - Just install it here.

95
00:03:23,663 --> 00:03:25,093
Hold on. Let me keep the door open.

96
00:03:25,963 --> 00:03:27,333
My gosh. No.

97
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,003
- I can't do it. - What's wrong?

98
00:03:29,663 --> 00:03:31,933
(Behind the entrance door, there are...)

99
00:03:32,533 --> 00:03:34,773
- See? - No way.

100
00:03:35,403 --> 00:03:37,242
People often assume that they can use the elevator...

101
00:03:37,243 --> 00:03:39,542
- directly from the parking lot. - Right.

102
00:03:39,543 --> 00:03:40,942
- That's right. - Who would have thought...

103
00:03:40,943 --> 00:03:42,112
- there would be stairs? - Right.

104
00:03:42,113 --> 00:03:44,082
You'll have to move it to Bum June's house anyway.

105
00:03:44,083 --> 00:03:45,242
The two of you...

106
00:03:45,243 --> 00:03:46,713
Hyun Moo will move it for you.

107
00:03:48,183 --> 00:03:50,483
- Hold on. We should... - Wait.

108
00:03:51,983 --> 00:03:53,253
I'll lift it from here.

109
00:03:53,723 --> 00:03:55,523
All right. One, two, three.

110
00:03:56,063 --> 00:03:57,792
(Struggling)

111
00:03:57,793 --> 00:03:58,993
We got it.

112
00:03:59,933 --> 00:04:01,662
(It's even difficult to lift it over the threshold.)

113
00:04:01,663 --> 00:04:04,063
- Hold on. This... My gosh. - We must carry them separately.

114
00:04:04,763 --> 00:04:06,403
- Not at once, right? - What?

115
00:04:06,573 --> 00:04:07,673
- Should we carry them at once? - At once?

116
00:04:08,073 --> 00:04:09,103
No, right?

117
00:04:09,503 --> 00:04:10,942
- I think we can do it. - What?

118
00:04:10,943 --> 00:04:12,442
- Let's do it in one go. - Yes. I think we can do it.

119
00:04:12,443 --> 00:04:13,612
- You can support me from the back. - It might be possible...

120
00:04:13,613 --> 00:04:14,812
- since there are two of them. - Exactly.

121
00:04:14,813 --> 00:04:15,843
It must be possible.

122
00:04:16,513 --> 00:04:17,542
(Strong thighs)

123
00:04:17,543 --> 00:04:19,182
Right. He's got strong thighs.

124
00:04:19,183 --> 00:04:21,383
(Massive arm muscles)

125
00:04:22,253 --> 00:04:23,322
(I'm a strong man, Ahn Jae Hyeon.)

126
00:04:23,323 --> 00:04:24,923
- You look great. - You're a real man.

127
00:04:25,383 --> 00:04:26,853
- A real man. - You're Thor.

128
00:04:27,923 --> 00:04:29,663
- You've been working out, right? - Of course.

129
00:04:29,793 --> 00:04:31,463
- Wait. But I can't see ahead. - Okay.

130
00:04:31,923 --> 00:04:33,862
Wait.

131
00:04:33,863 --> 00:04:35,533
(Wait.)

132
00:04:36,863 --> 00:04:38,462
- Is it going up? - Yes, you're doing a good job.

133
00:04:38,463 --> 00:04:40,603
Hyun Moo, wait.

134
00:04:41,003 --> 00:04:42,702
(They stop only after going up one step.)

135
00:04:42,703 --> 00:04:44,673
Keep going.

136
00:04:45,043 --> 00:04:47,543
No, don't!

137
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:53,613
(A shocking fall of Thor?)

138
00:04:53,983 --> 00:04:56,022
- Both of you are awful at this. - That's so true.

139
00:04:56,023 --> 00:04:57,582
- We should've separated them. - You should've separated them.

140
00:04:57,583 --> 00:04:59,822
- You've never done manual work. - Seriously.

141
00:04:59,823 --> 00:05:01,653
- Right. Look at his fair skin. - We wanted to do it in one go.

142
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:04,093
When I tried to lift it up, the oven rack hit my shins.

143
00:05:04,323 --> 00:05:06,032
- Right. Look how tall it is. - That's why?

144
00:05:06,033 --> 00:05:07,392
- You can't move them in one go. - No way.

145
00:05:07,393 --> 00:05:08,692
- My gosh. - That's not possible, right?

146
00:05:08,693 --> 00:05:09,902
It kept hitting my shins too.

147
00:05:09,903 --> 00:05:11,833
I somehow hurt my arm that day. It's still bruised.

148
00:05:12,063 --> 00:05:13,873
- My goodness. - It got bruised that day.

149
00:05:14,333 --> 00:05:15,333
My gosh.

150
00:05:15,334 --> 00:05:16,902
I thought you were getting an electric shock.

151
00:05:16,903 --> 00:05:19,003
(It's expected of Thor.)

152
00:05:19,813 --> 00:05:20,873
Keep going. No, don't!

153
00:05:21,173 --> 00:05:23,313
(Lightning)

154
00:05:23,483 --> 00:05:25,883
- Put it down. - Let's put it down.

155
00:05:26,083 --> 00:05:27,182
- Is this too much for you? - It's...

156
00:05:27,183 --> 00:05:29,082
No, it's not. But can you go up?

157
00:05:29,083 --> 00:05:31,022
- It's hard because of the incline. - Are you serious?

158
00:05:31,023 --> 00:05:32,523
It's harder for the guy in the back.

159
00:05:33,053 --> 00:05:34,092
Wait.

160
00:05:34,093 --> 00:05:35,222
(What do we do with this?)

161
00:05:35,223 --> 00:05:37,462
Then let's carry it up sideways.

162
00:05:37,463 --> 00:05:39,133
- How? - Let's go horizontal.

163
00:05:39,833 --> 00:05:41,833
- There's not enough space. - Really?

164
00:05:42,093 --> 00:05:44,732
Or should we carry it up diagonally?

165
00:05:44,733 --> 00:05:45,833
Wait.

166
00:05:46,733 --> 00:05:48,333
- Do you have enough space? - Can you go up?

167
00:05:49,943 --> 00:05:51,073
We can't.

168
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:53,472
(Giving up quickly)

169
00:05:53,473 --> 00:05:54,642
(Struggling)

170
00:05:54,643 --> 00:05:56,643
- You should move them separately. - No.

171
00:05:57,313 --> 00:05:58,683
Jae Hyeon is really weak.

172
00:05:58,983 --> 00:06:00,183
It was a tough day.

173
00:06:00,483 --> 00:06:01,653
There was a time...

174
00:06:02,183 --> 00:06:03,883
Jae Hyeon was really fit.

175
00:06:04,383 --> 00:06:05,723
It could've worked if he was still fit.

176
00:06:05,853 --> 00:06:07,253
But he went back to his old days.

177
00:06:07,553 --> 00:06:09,392
Muscles are so merciless.

178
00:06:09,393 --> 00:06:10,923
- They're gone without any exercise. - Exactly.

179
00:06:11,363 --> 00:06:12,363
Let's carry them one at a time.

180
00:06:12,364 --> 00:06:13,492
- One at a time? - Let's move the oven first.

181
00:06:13,493 --> 00:06:14,493
- The oven first? - Yes.

182
00:06:14,494 --> 00:06:15,633
- Should I carry this first? - There's no way around it.

183
00:06:15,763 --> 00:06:16,903
- Can you lift it? One, two. - I can.

184
00:06:17,633 --> 00:06:19,333
- I got this. - We should've done this first.

185
00:06:20,073 --> 00:06:22,372
- That's true. - Hey, we could've done this first.

186
00:06:22,373 --> 00:06:23,772
Right. You can move it one at a time.

187
00:06:23,773 --> 00:06:24,942
- We could've done it first. - I see.

188
00:06:24,943 --> 00:06:26,972
Obviously. Why would you want to carry the rack with it?

189
00:06:26,973 --> 00:06:28,613
It was so much easier then.

190
00:06:28,773 --> 00:06:29,912
You guys are so clueless.

191
00:06:29,913 --> 00:06:31,083
(Sighing)

192
00:06:31,883 --> 00:06:32,883
(Grunting)

193
00:06:35,213 --> 00:06:37,223
- I'll get the rack. I can do it. - No.

194
00:06:37,553 --> 00:06:38,653
This is light.

195
00:06:39,223 --> 00:06:40,353
Then try moving it on your own.

196
00:06:40,853 --> 00:06:42,663
- This is good. I can do it. - You're good.

197
00:06:42,893 --> 00:06:44,592
- Then you can move the rack. - That's light.

198
00:06:44,593 --> 00:06:45,593
Right.

199
00:06:46,593 --> 00:06:48,162
We should've done that from the start.

200
00:06:48,163 --> 00:06:49,633
(We should've done that from the start.)

201
00:06:49,863 --> 00:06:51,563
- One, two, three. - Two...

202
00:06:52,163 --> 00:06:53,273
That's good.

203
00:06:53,673 --> 00:06:54,903
- That's easy. - All right.

204
00:06:55,073 --> 00:06:56,202
- All done. - Okay.

205
00:06:56,203 --> 00:06:57,203
We got it.

206
00:06:57,204 --> 00:06:58,742
- Did we align them well? Yes. - Yes.

207
00:06:58,743 --> 00:07:00,912
Well done.

208
00:07:00,913 --> 00:07:03,383
(Exhausted)

209
00:07:04,143 --> 00:07:05,742
If your building didn't have an elevator...

210
00:07:05,743 --> 00:07:06,783
No way.

211
00:07:07,013 --> 00:07:08,053
I would've given up, right?

212
00:07:08,653 --> 00:07:10,282
One. Okay.

213
00:07:10,283 --> 00:07:11,753
I can't believe I'm going to your house.

214
00:07:11,883 --> 00:07:13,353
- This is your first time, right? - Yes.

215
00:07:15,093 --> 00:07:17,123
Hold on. Can it fit through? There's another door inside.

216
00:07:17,923 --> 00:07:19,023
Another door?

217
00:07:19,193 --> 00:07:20,593
What a headache.

218
00:07:21,063 --> 00:07:23,063
- Wait. Can it fit through the side? - Another door?

219
00:07:23,863 --> 00:07:25,763
- Should we even try? - Should we?

220
00:07:26,103 --> 00:07:27,673
- Wait. I think it will fit through. - My gosh, no.

221
00:07:28,333 --> 00:07:29,402
Here it goes.

222
00:07:29,403 --> 00:07:31,472
(Let's try pushing it in.)

223
00:07:31,473 --> 00:07:33,243
- I got it. - It can fit through?

224
00:07:33,443 --> 00:07:35,013
- No way. - It won't.

225
00:07:35,543 --> 00:07:36,612
One, two, three.

226
00:07:36,613 --> 00:07:37,713
(Lifting)

227
00:07:38,043 --> 00:07:39,113
It's stuck.

228
00:07:39,253 --> 00:07:40,413
- Right. It can't fit through. - It won't.

229
00:07:41,813 --> 00:07:43,323
- We have to remove the door. - Can you do it?

230
00:07:44,653 --> 00:07:46,122
(It's so hard to bring it into the house.)

231
00:07:46,123 --> 00:07:47,523
- Seriously. - I was so stressed by that point.

232
00:07:48,423 --> 00:07:50,062
(Rattling)

233
00:07:50,063 --> 00:07:51,092
You can do it right away.

234
00:07:51,093 --> 00:07:52,223
I saw the workers remove it once.

235
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:54,193
But I didn't see them putting it back.

236
00:07:55,433 --> 00:07:56,633
- Putting it back... - That should be easy.

237
00:07:57,463 --> 00:07:58,762
- Let's do it. - One, two.

238
00:07:58,763 --> 00:07:59,832
Three.

239
00:07:59,833 --> 00:08:01,702
(They finally bring the oven inside the house.)

240
00:08:01,703 --> 00:08:03,772
Hey. Okay. I got it.

241
00:08:03,773 --> 00:08:04,773
(They finally bring the oven inside the house.)

242
00:08:06,113 --> 00:08:07,612
(Exhausted)

243
00:08:07,613 --> 00:08:09,243
It's like watching "Pat and Mat."

244
00:08:11,413 --> 00:08:12,543
Gosh, I'm sweating.

245
00:08:12,783 --> 00:08:14,083
Why are you sweating so much?

246
00:08:15,313 --> 00:08:17,383
What's wrong with you? You're out of shape now?

247
00:08:18,053 --> 00:08:20,253
- Where should I put this? - Where... I haven't decided yet.

248
00:08:20,893 --> 00:08:22,723
You're not going to use this, right?

249
00:08:23,023 --> 00:08:24,562
- Will you? - I doubt it.

250
00:08:24,563 --> 00:08:26,463
- No. It's for your friend, right? - Yes.

251
00:08:26,633 --> 00:08:29,262
It's better to shove it inside a room you don't use.

252
00:08:29,263 --> 00:08:30,303
Really?

253
00:08:30,463 --> 00:08:31,762
Let me give you a tour of the house.

254
00:08:31,763 --> 00:08:32,902
(Unused space in the house...)

255
00:08:32,903 --> 00:08:33,933
- All right. - My gosh.

256
00:08:35,433 --> 00:08:37,403
- What's this? Why do you have this? - This is my bedroom.

257
00:08:37,643 --> 00:08:39,142
- My gosh. How cute. - Goodness.

258
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:40,312
- Is it Anju? - Is Anju friendly?

259
00:08:40,313 --> 00:08:42,242
- Anju. It's been a while. - Look at you.

260
00:08:42,243 --> 00:08:43,313
Anju doesn't bite.

261
00:08:43,643 --> 00:08:45,983
- Look at you. - Anju.

262
00:08:46,113 --> 00:08:48,183
- How cute. - He's so cute.

263
00:08:48,313 --> 00:08:49,683
He looks like a marshmallow.

264
00:08:50,483 --> 00:08:51,923
- Do you want to hold him? - Yes.

265
00:08:52,083 --> 00:08:53,192
Like this.

266
00:08:53,193 --> 00:08:54,293
- Anju. - Right.

267
00:08:54,453 --> 00:08:56,423
- Anju. - How is it? Is he heavy?

268
00:08:56,623 --> 00:08:57,922
Anju. He's not heavy.

269
00:08:57,923 --> 00:09:00,863
- Right. He's slim. - Anju.

270
00:09:01,263 --> 00:09:02,292
He's not moving at all.

271
00:09:02,293 --> 00:09:04,563
He looks like a white DCC.

272
00:09:04,963 --> 00:09:06,003
I love him.

273
00:09:06,503 --> 00:09:08,673
I keep my clothes in this room.

274
00:09:09,373 --> 00:09:11,103
- I don't think I can put it here. - Anju.

275
00:09:11,273 --> 00:09:12,602
The oven is quite big.

276
00:09:12,603 --> 00:09:14,113
The oven was much bigger than I thought.

277
00:09:14,613 --> 00:09:16,313
- Since you're here... - Yes.

278
00:09:16,883 --> 00:09:18,813
There are some clothes I can't wear because they're small.

279
00:09:20,313 --> 00:09:22,853
What do you think? Take a look at this.

280
00:09:23,723 --> 00:09:25,553
It's the last piece of clothing from Givenchy I own.

281
00:09:26,053 --> 00:09:27,123
It's good, right?

282
00:09:27,323 --> 00:09:28,652
It's too tight on me. So I can't wear it.

283
00:09:28,653 --> 00:09:29,893
He suddenly lit up.

284
00:09:31,063 --> 00:09:32,392
I saved it for special occasions.

285
00:09:32,393 --> 00:09:33,733
(Let me try it on.)

286
00:09:34,463 --> 00:09:35,463
(My gosh, it's Givenchy!)

287
00:09:35,464 --> 00:09:37,563
- Because you bulked up? - Yes, so it's too tight on me.

288
00:09:37,933 --> 00:09:40,103
You can't throw out some clothes because they're from luxury brands.

289
00:09:40,403 --> 00:09:41,772
- This is good. - Do you like it?

290
00:09:41,773 --> 00:09:42,872
- My gosh. - Does it fit you?

291
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:44,173
Yes. It looks so good on me. Gosh.

292
00:09:44,473 --> 00:09:45,672
This is perfect for me.

293
00:09:45,673 --> 00:09:46,742
Doesn't it look great on me?

294
00:09:46,743 --> 00:09:48,112
(This is mine.)

295
00:09:48,113 --> 00:09:49,442
What do you think? Will you wear it or not?

296
00:09:49,443 --> 00:09:50,712
- I will. Yes. - It's a good jacket, right?

297
00:09:50,713 --> 00:09:53,112
- You can't take it back. - The jacket is layered. Look.

298
00:09:53,113 --> 00:09:54,953
- Forget it. It's Givenchy. - The jacket... Really?

299
00:09:55,713 --> 00:09:56,983
I'll give you the clothes hanger for it too.

300
00:09:57,053 --> 00:09:58,223
Yes. Thank you.

301
00:09:58,753 --> 00:10:00,893
Here you go. It feels good to have proper clothes hangers.

302
00:10:00,993 --> 00:10:02,153
The clothes hanger from Givenchy.

303
00:10:02,353 --> 00:10:04,463
- I don't own one from Givenchy. - Really?

304
00:10:04,563 --> 00:10:06,163
- You don't have one from Givenchy? - No, I don't.

305
00:10:06,363 --> 00:10:07,392
That's good then.

306
00:10:07,393 --> 00:10:08,563
- I'll hang it here for now. - Okay.

307
00:10:09,263 --> 00:10:10,533
You'll take it home.

308
00:10:12,633 --> 00:10:13,873
Why am I smelling curry?

309
00:10:13,933 --> 00:10:15,072
I made curry.

310
00:10:15,073 --> 00:10:16,403
- Why is everyone trying to feed me? - He's going to eat again?

311
00:10:17,643 --> 00:10:19,412
Let me take a look at this.

312
00:10:19,413 --> 00:10:21,112
I thought about placing this...

313
00:10:21,113 --> 00:10:22,783
- where my bicycle is. - Yes, that's a good spot too.

314
00:10:24,043 --> 00:10:26,252
It's your oven now. So don't ask me.

315
00:10:26,253 --> 00:10:27,283
The house...

316
00:10:27,553 --> 00:10:29,852
But when people come over, they will think that...

317
00:10:29,853 --> 00:10:32,283
- you're serious about cooking. - Really?

318
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:33,752
- When you bake bread with it, - Yes.

319
00:10:33,753 --> 00:10:35,322
- your house will smell like bread. - Really?

320
00:10:35,323 --> 00:10:36,922
- It's no joke? - The buttery smell...

321
00:10:36,923 --> 00:10:38,192
This looks like a nice spot.

322
00:10:38,193 --> 00:10:39,432
I can get an extension cord.

323
00:10:39,433 --> 00:10:40,993
- Right. - There's a window here.

324
00:10:41,193 --> 00:10:43,163
Right. It creates a lot of heat at the back.

325
00:10:43,233 --> 00:10:44,533
So it's better if it's open in the back.

326
00:10:45,263 --> 00:10:46,703
- I like it here for now. - Yes.

327
00:10:47,773 --> 00:10:49,572
- It's still in the same spot. - It is?

328
00:10:49,573 --> 00:10:51,042
- You can't put it anywhere else. - It's still there.

329
00:10:51,043 --> 00:10:52,243
So I move it and then put it back.

330
00:10:53,613 --> 00:10:56,983
There are trendy DCC from Seongsu. Do you know about them?

331
00:10:57,413 --> 00:10:58,483
- Yes. - Have you tried them?

332
00:10:58,643 --> 00:11:00,713
- Were you able to buy them? - No.

333
00:11:01,213 --> 00:11:02,923
Have you had DCC?

334
00:11:03,283 --> 00:11:04,323
I have.

335
00:11:04,753 --> 00:11:06,493
- I have. - But from a legit place?

336
00:11:06,853 --> 00:11:08,493
No, I don't think I had authentic ones.

337
00:11:08,893 --> 00:11:09,893
Do you know a good place for it?

338
00:11:10,093 --> 00:11:11,363
- Yes. - Where is it?

339
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,132
- I bought some. - What?

340
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:14,592
- I bought some. - You did?

341
00:11:14,593 --> 00:11:15,893
Yes. Sit down.

342
00:11:16,063 --> 00:11:17,403
You'll go crazy once you look at them.

343
00:11:18,633 --> 00:11:19,702
He will.

344
00:11:19,703 --> 00:11:21,803
- He will go crazy for sure. - I really thought he bought them.

345
00:11:22,633 --> 00:11:25,343
- I waited in line for a long time. - Really?

346
00:11:25,473 --> 00:11:27,943
I waited for 4 hours, but I could only buy 2.

347
00:11:29,713 --> 00:11:32,243
- Gosh, this is crazy. - Where did you buy them?

348
00:11:32,643 --> 00:11:34,013
In the basement food court of the department store.

349
00:11:34,283 --> 00:11:37,323
A high-end brand was doing a pop-up event there.

350
00:11:37,583 --> 00:11:39,493
- This is crazy, right? - That sounds convincing.

351
00:11:39,853 --> 00:11:40,892
Each cookie cost 40 dollars.

352
00:11:40,893 --> 00:11:42,393
- It cost 40 dollars? - I could only buy 2.

353
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:44,622
And I bought the last two.

354
00:11:44,623 --> 00:11:46,293
(Falling for the lie)

355
00:11:46,763 --> 00:11:48,692
- I can't wait to try it. - It looks so good too.

356
00:11:48,693 --> 00:11:51,033
- I want to try it. - I could picture him buying them.

357
00:11:51,233 --> 00:11:52,733
- That's understandable. - Seriously.

358
00:11:53,073 --> 00:11:54,132
He would've bought them...

359
00:11:54,133 --> 00:11:55,173
- even if they cost 400 dollars. - Right.

360
00:11:55,903 --> 00:11:57,143
- As long as they're trendy. - As long as they're trendy.

361
00:11:57,303 --> 00:11:58,403
As long as they're trendy.

362
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,713
- Let's have this after curry. - Let's have some curry.

363
00:12:00,943 --> 00:12:02,273
- I saw you... - Yes.

364
00:12:02,573 --> 00:12:05,042
having curry in the waiting room.

365
00:12:05,043 --> 00:12:06,283
So I made curry.

366
00:12:06,883 --> 00:12:08,013
He's so thoughtful.

367
00:12:08,453 --> 00:12:09,553
Where should I sit? There?

368
00:12:09,753 --> 00:12:11,053
Wherever you want.

369
00:12:11,653 --> 00:12:12,753
Let's eat it on the sofa.

370
00:12:13,053 --> 00:12:14,323
- Should we? - Yes.

371
00:12:14,853 --> 00:12:16,622
Let's see how good Jae Hyeon's curry tastes.

372
00:12:16,623 --> 00:12:17,963
My gosh. It's very good.

373
00:12:19,763 --> 00:12:20,863
Anju.

374
00:12:21,933 --> 00:12:23,863
(Looking indifferent)

375
00:12:28,273 --> 00:12:29,903
(Poking)

376
00:12:30,573 --> 00:12:31,972
You don't like that.

377
00:12:31,973 --> 00:12:33,513
(Adorable)

378
00:12:33,773 --> 00:12:34,813
Come at me.

379
00:12:35,443 --> 00:12:36,483
(Meowing)

380
00:12:36,743 --> 00:12:38,442
(Kitty punches)

381
00:12:38,443 --> 00:12:40,253
My gosh. You're upset now?

382
00:12:40,953 --> 00:12:42,013
It's ready.

383
00:12:42,983 --> 00:12:44,282
- Gosh, that looks good. - That looks great.

384
00:12:44,283 --> 00:12:45,553
Homemade curry.

385
00:12:46,453 --> 00:12:48,592
I only added meat and potatoes.

386
00:12:48,593 --> 00:12:51,092
Adding a lot of meat and potatoes is an adult privilege...

387
00:12:51,093 --> 00:12:52,893
- That's right. No carrots. - since we can make it ourselves.

388
00:12:53,893 --> 00:12:55,332
- The scallion kimchi. - You know.

389
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:56,533
(A plate of scallion kimchi to eat with curry)

390
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,062
The scallion kimchi looks amazing.

391
00:12:58,063 --> 00:12:59,572
What do you think? It's got a nice color, right?

392
00:12:59,573 --> 00:13:01,603
(A curry meal for President Jun who came for the post-sales service)

393
00:13:01,803 --> 00:13:03,443
- Thank you for the meal. - Enjoy.

394
00:13:03,643 --> 00:13:04,773
I hope you like it.

395
00:13:05,943 --> 00:13:08,213
(Taking a big spoonful of the curry)

396
00:13:09,813 --> 00:13:11,142
What do you think? Is it good?

397
00:13:11,143 --> 00:13:12,913
Moving the oven was a tough job. Please eat a lot.

398
00:13:14,153 --> 00:13:16,883
(He eats it with the scallion kimchi this time.)

399
00:13:17,383 --> 00:13:18,723
(Look at this guy.)

400
00:13:18,953 --> 00:13:20,193
Isn't the scallion kimchi really good?

401
00:13:21,753 --> 00:13:22,893
The scallion kimchi.

402
00:13:22,993 --> 00:13:25,223
- That's so good. - Gosh, it looks so tasty.

403
00:13:25,523 --> 00:13:26,593
I'm so hungry.

404
00:13:27,393 --> 00:13:29,092
The pork is really tender.

405
00:13:29,093 --> 00:13:30,862
- It melts in your mouth. Good. - Yes.

406
00:13:30,863 --> 00:13:32,203
I made it yesterday on purpose.

407
00:13:32,563 --> 00:13:33,773
It's better the day after.

408
00:13:33,973 --> 00:13:34,973
You made it tenderer...

409
00:13:34,973 --> 00:13:35,973
- by cooking it the day before? - Yes.

410
00:13:36,643 --> 00:13:38,103
You know it's better the day after, right?

411
00:13:38,173 --> 00:13:39,502
- It was so good. - That's so true.

412
00:13:39,503 --> 00:13:40,573
Of course.

413
00:13:43,243 --> 00:13:45,243
My gosh, that looks so good.

414
00:13:45,713 --> 00:13:47,183
It's been a while since I had curry.

415
00:13:47,353 --> 00:13:48,483
- Same here. - Yes.

416
00:13:49,483 --> 00:13:52,523
(Shockingly, he had ramyeon and a plate of sushi before this.)

417
00:13:52,883 --> 00:13:54,523
He ate so much that day.

418
00:13:54,723 --> 00:13:56,223
He seemed to enjoy it.

419
00:13:56,393 --> 00:13:57,562
His curry is good.

420
00:13:57,563 --> 00:13:59,293
(Approving it as good curry)

421
00:14:00,063 --> 00:14:01,463
My gosh, you're good at cooking.

422
00:14:02,733 --> 00:14:04,002
Hey, it's so good?

423
00:14:04,003 --> 00:14:05,063
Did you finish it?

424
00:14:06,033 --> 00:14:07,103
Dubai chewy cookies?

425
00:14:08,403 --> 00:14:11,103
In the basement food court... My gosh, seriously.

426
00:14:11,903 --> 00:14:14,913
I've never waited in line for four hours for some cookies.

427
00:14:16,143 --> 00:14:20,583
(Rummaging through)

428
00:14:21,413 --> 00:14:22,912
Should I bring a cute plate?

429
00:14:22,913 --> 00:14:25,153
- You should. They're so fancy. - Right.

430
00:14:25,523 --> 00:14:26,593
He's really looking forward to it.

431
00:14:27,523 --> 00:14:28,723
I really did.

432
00:14:29,293 --> 00:14:31,393
The people behind me got so angry.

433
00:14:31,793 --> 00:14:33,362
- Because you were the last one? - "Then why did I wait in line?"

434
00:14:33,363 --> 00:14:34,663
"You should've let us know."

435
00:14:35,133 --> 00:14:36,633
They were angry they wasted time waiting in line.

436
00:14:37,963 --> 00:14:40,373
(Opening up)

437
00:14:40,833 --> 00:14:42,073
Do you need a fork?

438
00:14:42,873 --> 00:14:43,902
We need forks and knives.

439
00:14:43,903 --> 00:14:46,773
This bakery's cookies are quite big.

440
00:14:47,713 --> 00:14:49,243
Should I go with an elegant vibe?

441
00:14:49,613 --> 00:14:50,883
He got his hopes up.

442
00:14:52,113 --> 00:14:53,252
(He's serious about DCC.)

443
00:14:53,253 --> 00:14:55,113
You must really like DCC.

444
00:14:55,713 --> 00:14:57,052
- He was looking forward to it. - Right.

445
00:14:57,053 --> 00:14:58,122
He's grabbing milk too.

446
00:14:58,123 --> 00:14:59,153
(Clueless of the lie, he grabs milk too.)

447
00:14:59,753 --> 00:15:01,723
You brought milk too. You know the perfect pairing.

448
00:15:03,393 --> 00:15:04,593
I can't wait.

449
00:15:05,523 --> 00:15:06,732
As for the plate,

450
00:15:06,733 --> 00:15:08,163
- There you go. - I got us a red one.

451
00:15:08,363 --> 00:15:09,833
- My gosh. - Here's your individual plate.

452
00:15:10,133 --> 00:15:12,762
I'm so curious. My expectations are really high now.

453
00:15:12,763 --> 00:15:13,772
Really?

454
00:15:13,773 --> 00:15:16,602
But Jae Hyeon is such a nice guy.

455
00:15:16,603 --> 00:15:18,573
He's not the type to be direct.

456
00:15:18,673 --> 00:15:20,613
He would've said they were tasty even if they were made of poop.

457
00:15:21,013 --> 00:15:22,842
- I'm curious about his reaction... - Same here.

458
00:15:22,843 --> 00:15:24,142
- the moment Hyun Moo takes it out. - I'm also very curious.

459
00:15:24,143 --> 00:15:25,413
I wonder how he'll react.

460
00:15:25,943 --> 00:15:28,213
This place has unique packaging.

461
00:15:28,813 --> 00:15:30,952
I thought, "The original ones are indeed different."

462
00:15:30,953 --> 00:15:33,152
- Other places make it look pretty. - Right.

463
00:15:33,153 --> 00:15:34,423
But this place... Look.

464
00:15:34,693 --> 00:15:35,852
- I... - Is it just wrapped in paper?

465
00:15:35,853 --> 00:15:38,192
Pretty much. Their cookies are so rustic like an old restaurant.

466
00:15:38,193 --> 00:15:40,393
- Like the old-school fried chicken? - Right. The old-school chicken.

467
00:15:41,363 --> 00:15:43,102
(Looking forward to it)

468
00:15:43,103 --> 00:15:44,732
What kind of bakery makes rustic DCC?

469
00:15:44,733 --> 00:15:46,103
He's so kind.

470
00:15:46,873 --> 00:15:48,302
- Close your eyes. - Really?

471
00:15:48,303 --> 00:15:50,273
- Buying them wasn't easy. - Okay.

472
00:15:50,603 --> 00:15:52,303
- Don't open your eyes. - You'll put it on my hand?

473
00:15:53,213 --> 00:15:54,312
I'll put it in front of you.

474
00:15:54,313 --> 00:15:55,742
(Rustling)

475
00:15:55,743 --> 00:15:56,882
Gosh, it sounds...

476
00:15:56,883 --> 00:15:58,282
(Gosh, it even sounds different.)

477
00:15:58,283 --> 00:16:00,753
What about the sound? How did it sound?

478
00:16:00,913 --> 00:16:02,612
- It sounded fancy. - What are you talking about?

479
00:16:02,613 --> 00:16:03,982
- It was just a plastic bag. - It was from a plastic bag.

480
00:16:03,983 --> 00:16:05,052
How's that fancy?

481
00:16:05,053 --> 00:16:06,053
I was already hooked.

482
00:16:07,493 --> 00:16:09,192
- Gosh, it sounds... - It's different, right?

483
00:16:09,193 --> 00:16:11,092
- I can hear it. - The packaging was classy.

484
00:16:11,093 --> 00:16:13,493
- It sounds like paper parchment. - That's it.

485
00:16:14,093 --> 00:16:16,602
- That's the authentic version. - You waited in line for this.

486
00:16:16,603 --> 00:16:17,733
Can I open my eyes?

487
00:16:18,363 --> 00:16:22,203
One, two, three.

488
00:16:24,543 --> 00:16:28,043
(The authentic DCC is revealed!)

489
00:16:28,707 --> 00:16:30,546
- That's the authentic version. - Can I open my eyes?

490
00:16:30,547 --> 00:16:32,207
One, two, three.

491
00:16:33,317 --> 00:16:37,017
(Gasping)

492
00:16:45,357 --> 00:16:47,027
My mind went blank.

493
00:16:47,457 --> 00:16:48,856
From this clip, I realized once again...

494
00:16:48,857 --> 00:16:50,927
- that you're such a nice guy. - Why do you say that?

495
00:16:51,097 --> 00:16:53,296
- You were ready to act impressed. - Right.

496
00:16:53,297 --> 00:16:54,936
- "I should act impressed first." - I see.

497
00:16:54,937 --> 00:16:56,806
He was about to frown,

498
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,166
but decided not to.

499
00:16:58,167 --> 00:16:59,566
- Then he's trying to smile. - Right.

500
00:16:59,567 --> 00:17:01,637
His facial expression in that split second is funny.

501
00:17:03,077 --> 00:17:04,106
(Gasping)

502
00:17:04,107 --> 00:17:06,107
(What do you think?)

503
00:17:07,217 --> 00:17:09,676
(This is the authentic version of DCC?)

504
00:17:09,677 --> 00:17:11,687
(Trying to hold back his laughter)

505
00:17:13,557 --> 00:17:14,557
Really?

506
00:17:18,257 --> 00:17:19,456
(To call it a high-end DCC, it looks quite sloppy.)

507
00:17:19,457 --> 00:17:21,227
- "Really?" - "Really?"

508
00:17:21,697 --> 00:17:23,867
I made it since 7am this morning.

509
00:17:24,297 --> 00:17:26,327
- Wait, you made this? - Yes.

510
00:17:26,837 --> 00:17:28,266
My expectations are completely ruined.

511
00:17:28,267 --> 00:17:29,397
What? No.

512
00:17:29,797 --> 00:17:31,166
Let me tell you something.

513
00:17:31,167 --> 00:17:32,666
- You know Hue, right? - Yes.

514
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:34,176
- He asked for one more. - Really?

515
00:17:34,177 --> 00:17:37,547
He said it was better than the one he had in Busan.

516
00:17:38,507 --> 00:17:39,847
I'm curious about how it tastes, though.

517
00:17:41,077 --> 00:17:42,477
- Let me taste it. - Okay.

518
00:17:43,317 --> 00:17:45,647
(Rustling)

519
00:17:46,287 --> 00:17:48,487
(Oh, my)

520
00:17:49,457 --> 00:17:50,687
It sort of looks like gaetteok too.

521
00:17:52,287 --> 00:17:53,526
You're lucky it's not dog poop.

522
00:17:53,527 --> 00:17:55,626
You know gaetteok? The one made with mugwort.

523
00:17:55,627 --> 00:17:57,597
- It's so good. - What happened to the wrapper?

524
00:18:00,367 --> 00:18:02,266
Your finishing touch looks off.

525
00:18:02,267 --> 00:18:03,936
- What? It looks like pursed lips. - No.

526
00:18:03,937 --> 00:18:05,767
It looks like Siru's anus.

527
00:18:06,267 --> 00:18:07,307
Right.

528
00:18:08,037 --> 00:18:09,576
- I'll cut this in half. - Check the inside.

529
00:18:09,577 --> 00:18:10,976
Check how much pistachio spread I added.

530
00:18:10,977 --> 00:18:12,046
(He cuts it into bite-sized pieces.)

531
00:18:12,047 --> 00:18:13,317
- Gosh. - See?

532
00:18:14,147 --> 00:18:15,846
When I sliced it, I got that crunchy texture.

533
00:18:15,847 --> 00:18:17,347
Of course. That's kadayif.

534
00:18:19,217 --> 00:18:20,556
You know that kadayif looks like...

535
00:18:20,557 --> 00:18:21,586
- thin noodles. - Right.

536
00:18:21,587 --> 00:18:22,656
But my kadayif looks like this.

537
00:18:22,657 --> 00:18:23,757
- They're long? - They're like kalguksu noodles.

538
00:18:24,357 --> 00:18:27,426
Slicing the cookie felt like I was stepping on first snow.

539
00:18:27,427 --> 00:18:28,826
- That's right. It's crunchy. - Yes.

540
00:18:28,827 --> 00:18:30,367
He said it was like stepping on first snow.

541
00:18:30,627 --> 00:18:32,726
How's that anything like stepping on first snow?

542
00:18:32,727 --> 00:18:34,337
Gosh, he's so kind.

543
00:18:35,937 --> 00:18:37,937
- The title is "First Snow." - Really?

544
00:18:38,707 --> 00:18:40,406
- Oh, my. - Oh, my.

545
00:18:40,407 --> 00:18:42,276
My gosh. You know you have to stretch it out like this.

546
00:18:42,277 --> 00:18:43,977
Of course. That's why it's called a chewy cookie.

547
00:18:44,947 --> 00:18:46,077
Gosh, this is crazy.

548
00:18:46,877 --> 00:18:47,916
I'll try it.

549
00:18:47,917 --> 00:18:49,176
(Putting it in his mouth without any hesitation)

550
00:18:49,177 --> 00:18:50,847
His initial reaction is important.

551
00:18:51,847 --> 00:18:52,987
(Crunchy)

552
00:18:53,317 --> 00:18:54,886
My gosh. It sounds like he's eating a real cookie.

553
00:18:54,887 --> 00:18:56,187
It sounds like you're eating radish kimchi.

554
00:18:58,027 --> 00:18:59,127
Is this kadayif?

555
00:19:01,497 --> 00:19:04,067
(Confused by the thick kadayif he's never had before)

556
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,466
Is this kadayif?

557
00:19:06,467 --> 00:19:12,037
(Chocking)

558
00:19:12,337 --> 00:19:14,337
- The glutinous rice... Oh, my bad. - Okay.

559
00:19:14,677 --> 00:19:16,946
- The marshmallows... - They got stuck in my mouth.

560
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:17,947
Right.

561
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:20,246
- I bet it got stuck on your throat. - Right.

562
00:19:20,247 --> 00:19:22,116
People who had it know the difference.

563
00:19:22,117 --> 00:19:24,186
- Their attitude is different. - Of course.

564
00:19:24,187 --> 00:19:25,187
It's different.

565
00:19:26,717 --> 00:19:27,787
Is this...

566
00:19:27,887 --> 00:19:29,386
(Snorting)

567
00:19:29,387 --> 00:19:30,987
(Choking)

568
00:19:31,827 --> 00:19:33,696
It's stuck on your throat, right?

569
00:19:33,697 --> 00:19:34,697
Yes.

570
00:19:34,957 --> 00:19:36,457
Hence the name, "chewy."

571
00:19:36,627 --> 00:19:39,097
It once got stuck in my throat that I couldn't talk.

572
00:19:39,727 --> 00:19:41,097
(Burping)

573
00:19:41,397 --> 00:19:42,537
You have indigestion, right?

574
00:19:43,637 --> 00:19:46,267
(Quickly washing down the chewy cookie with milk)

575
00:19:46,907 --> 00:19:48,976
It's hard to wash it down. It's so sticky.

576
00:19:48,977 --> 00:19:50,577
- Do you have indigestion? - By the way...

577
00:19:51,677 --> 00:19:52,707
(Crunchy)

578
00:19:54,877 --> 00:19:57,187
Did that crunchy sound come from your throat?

579
00:19:57,587 --> 00:19:59,247
It sounds like he's chewing on amalgam.

580
00:19:59,747 --> 00:20:02,156
When I was chewing it, there was a crunchy bit.

581
00:20:02,157 --> 00:20:03,456
I thought I was going to lose my tooth.

582
00:20:03,457 --> 00:20:04,557
(It's not easy to chew down the kadayif.)

583
00:20:04,657 --> 00:20:08,557
You know the cereal people eat in the morning?

584
00:20:08,827 --> 00:20:10,527
I don't like soggy cereal.

585
00:20:10,597 --> 00:20:11,826
- That's the worst. - I really like...

586
00:20:11,827 --> 00:20:13,966
that crunchy texture when I take a bite of it.

587
00:20:13,967 --> 00:20:15,936
And your cookie is crunchy. I'm serious.

588
00:20:15,937 --> 00:20:17,107
- It's good, right? - Yes.

589
00:20:17,907 --> 00:20:19,566
- It's like a scorched rice cookie. - Right.

590
00:20:19,567 --> 00:20:21,276
It's not a Dubai chewy cookie. It's a Moo chewy cookie.

591
00:20:21,277 --> 00:20:23,006
Even when you have it three days later,

592
00:20:23,007 --> 00:20:24,106
- it will still have... - It's...

593
00:20:24,107 --> 00:20:25,406
the glass-shard texture.

594
00:20:25,407 --> 00:20:27,446
(Smug)

595
00:20:27,447 --> 00:20:28,917
(Impressed)

596
00:20:29,747 --> 00:20:31,017
Honestly, this is good.

597
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:32,886
It's just that I sound like a fool when I speak after eating it.

598
00:20:32,887 --> 00:20:34,057
It messes up your pronunciation.

599
00:20:34,117 --> 00:20:35,516
- Honestly, it's good. - It's good, right?

600
00:20:35,517 --> 00:20:37,986
I think the glass shard cut off his tongue.

601
00:20:37,987 --> 00:20:39,887
(I think the glass shard cut off his tongue.)

602
00:20:40,457 --> 00:20:41,657
I'd pay money for this.

603
00:20:41,827 --> 00:20:42,927
- Right? - Yes.

604
00:20:43,057 --> 00:20:44,196
- Do you mean it? - I'd pay money for it.

605
00:20:44,197 --> 00:20:45,667
Really? How much would you pay for this?

606
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:48,696
If you use different packaging, not this plastic bag,

607
00:20:48,697 --> 00:20:50,467
- Yes. - I'd pay 11.5 dollars.

608
00:20:51,207 --> 00:20:52,506
- Like a craft burger. - Then...

609
00:20:52,507 --> 00:20:53,777
The packaging was pretty bad, right?

610
00:20:55,237 --> 00:20:56,306
Because of the size?

611
00:20:56,307 --> 00:20:58,307
He used a lot of ingredients for that.

612
00:20:58,347 --> 00:21:00,046
It was good because it wasn't too sweet.

613
00:21:00,047 --> 00:21:02,016
- Right. - It wasn't sweet, so it was good.

614
00:21:02,017 --> 00:21:03,686
Everyone is complimenting it.

615
00:21:03,687 --> 00:21:04,987
I'm curious.

616
00:21:06,717 --> 00:21:09,287
Thank you for bringing the oven. Move on to your next delivery.

617
00:21:09,657 --> 00:21:11,486
- He wasn't done. - You have more things to deliver?

618
00:21:11,487 --> 00:21:13,556
- There's more? - That was past 9pm.

619
00:21:13,557 --> 00:21:15,027
- What? - There's another one?

620
00:21:16,097 --> 00:21:18,227
You didn't have to see me off.

621
00:21:18,967 --> 00:21:21,367
(He didn't forget to grab the jacket from G brand.)

622
00:21:22,367 --> 00:21:24,007
- I'll use it well. - Thank you for the meal.

623
00:21:24,867 --> 00:21:26,437
- Bye. Thank you. - Bye.

624
00:21:26,837 --> 00:21:28,337
It's 9pm now.

625
00:21:28,937 --> 00:21:31,046
I'll arrive at my last stop...

626
00:21:31,047 --> 00:21:32,576
at 9:30pm.

627
00:21:32,577 --> 00:21:33,747
At 9:30pm?

628
00:21:34,417 --> 00:21:36,516
It's like you're going around to give out wedding invitations.

629
00:21:36,517 --> 00:21:37,717
You've been out all day.

630
00:21:40,487 --> 00:21:44,427
(He's calling someone while driving.)

631
00:21:44,487 --> 00:21:45,557
Hello.

632
00:21:46,187 --> 00:21:47,296
- Sung Hwan. - Sung Hwan?

633
00:21:47,297 --> 00:21:48,297
- It's Sung Hwan? - Hey.

634
00:21:48,298 --> 00:21:50,366
I'll arrive at 9:24pm. Okay?

635
00:21:50,367 --> 00:21:52,427
- Okay. I got it. - Okay.

636
00:21:52,597 --> 00:21:54,267
What other item needs after-sales service?

637
00:21:54,467 --> 00:21:55,836
It was the most important one.

638
00:21:55,837 --> 00:21:57,036
(The most important after-sales service for Sung Hwan)

639
00:21:57,037 --> 00:21:58,307
It's the most important one?

640
00:21:58,737 --> 00:21:59,967
It has something to do with you too.

641
00:22:00,107 --> 00:22:01,107
Me?

642
00:22:02,037 --> 00:22:03,846
This is the place. I've arrived.

643
00:22:03,847 --> 00:22:05,207
(Finally,)

644
00:22:06,247 --> 00:22:08,446
(he arrives at Sung Hwan's house for the most important job.)

645
00:22:08,447 --> 00:22:09,817
You're good at parking.

646
00:22:10,177 --> 00:22:11,816
- He's so good at parking. - Yes.

647
00:22:11,817 --> 00:22:13,147
He's a great driver.

648
00:22:13,657 --> 00:22:14,717
My gosh, I'm full.

649
00:22:15,187 --> 00:22:16,256
I was so full that day.

650
00:22:16,257 --> 00:22:17,656
Wait, did you eat again at his house?

651
00:22:17,657 --> 00:22:19,227
- I'm going to Sung Hwan's house. - Right.

652
00:22:20,557 --> 00:22:22,097
My gosh. It's...

653
00:22:23,457 --> 00:22:24,667
night now.

654
00:22:25,267 --> 00:22:26,967
When you have a long day, you can think,

655
00:22:27,067 --> 00:22:28,367
"I'll sleep like a baby tonight."

656
00:22:29,037 --> 00:22:30,366
That lifts your spirit a bit.

657
00:22:30,367 --> 00:22:31,607
I always sleep like a baby.

658
00:22:34,007 --> 00:22:35,337
- I pass out every day. - Really?

659
00:22:36,407 --> 00:22:38,547
(I can sleep like a baby after this.)

660
00:22:38,847 --> 00:22:40,747
Gosh, there's no elevator.

661
00:22:41,677 --> 00:22:42,917
No elevator for me.

662
00:22:43,647 --> 00:22:44,886
(Walking up)

663
00:22:44,887 --> 00:22:46,087
Gosh, this is...

664
00:22:46,817 --> 00:22:49,157
(Sniffing)

665
00:22:49,817 --> 00:22:51,627
It must be the unit with the delicious smell, right?

666
00:22:51,827 --> 00:22:53,356
You could smell delicious food?

667
00:22:53,357 --> 00:22:55,897
All the units from the second floor and up smelled so good.

668
00:22:56,327 --> 00:22:57,927
I guess he prepared a lot of food.

669
00:22:58,997 --> 00:23:00,367
(Pushing up)

670
00:23:00,467 --> 00:23:01,836
(Beeping)

671
00:23:01,837 --> 00:23:02,937
Come here.

672
00:23:03,267 --> 00:23:04,267
No.

673
00:23:04,268 --> 00:23:05,767
- He's wearing an apron. - No.

674
00:23:06,207 --> 00:23:07,207
Who is it?

675
00:23:08,177 --> 00:23:09,177
Open up.

676
00:23:09,437 --> 00:23:11,107
He just got here.

677
00:23:11,447 --> 00:23:13,447
I thought your passcode was 1818.

678
00:23:13,747 --> 00:23:15,117
(Joking)

679
00:23:15,647 --> 00:23:18,247
Kkotbun.

680
00:23:18,617 --> 00:23:20,116
- Hyun Moo. - Kkotbun.

681
00:23:20,117 --> 00:23:21,886
- Gosh, she's excited. - Your shoes...

682
00:23:21,887 --> 00:23:22,887
Kkotbun.

683
00:23:22,888 --> 00:23:24,757
- Kkotbun. - You've never met Kkotbun, right?

684
00:23:25,357 --> 00:23:27,297
- Kkotbun. She likes me. - What's all that?

685
00:23:27,827 --> 00:23:29,656
- Gosh. - I'll show them to you later.

686
00:23:29,657 --> 00:23:30,996
- Hyun Moo. - Yes.

687
00:23:30,997 --> 00:23:32,167
Take a look.

688
00:23:32,527 --> 00:23:33,737
It's...

689
00:23:33,967 --> 00:23:36,166
- Okay. Play with Kkotbun first. - Kkotbun.

690
00:23:36,167 --> 00:23:38,267
(Moomoo, the dog expert, meets Kkotbun in person.)

691
00:23:38,967 --> 00:23:40,436
Kkotbun.

692
00:23:40,437 --> 00:23:42,636
- You... - Sung Hwan looks different today.

693
00:23:42,637 --> 00:23:43,976
He looks like a well-built housewife, right?

694
00:23:43,977 --> 00:23:45,547
(A well-built housewife)

695
00:23:45,947 --> 00:23:47,016
- Hyun Moo. - Yes.

696
00:23:47,017 --> 00:23:48,476
These are my favorite art pieces.

697
00:23:48,477 --> 00:23:50,946
As you can see in my house, I actually like art.

698
00:23:50,947 --> 00:23:53,047
- That's your taste in art. - Santorini.

699
00:23:53,287 --> 00:23:54,757
- Santorini. - Oh, this is Santorini.

700
00:23:55,157 --> 00:23:57,027
- It says, "taco," not Santorini. - Listen.

701
00:23:58,787 --> 00:23:59,987
He thinks it's Santorini if it's not Korea.

702
00:24:01,197 --> 00:24:02,796
Oh, this is Santorini. And...

703
00:24:02,797 --> 00:24:04,166
I have your painting, one of my favorites...

704
00:24:04,167 --> 00:24:05,567
along with my other favorite pieces.

705
00:24:06,327 --> 00:24:08,296
But I placed yours all the way in the front before everything.

706
00:24:08,297 --> 00:24:10,337
- Before everything. I like art. - You like art.

707
00:24:11,437 --> 00:24:13,837
The last stop of Moomoo's After-Sales Service is...

708
00:24:13,977 --> 00:24:16,237
the man who will get the Grand Award Air.

709
00:24:16,907 --> 00:24:18,107
It's Sung Hwan's house.

710
00:24:19,007 --> 00:24:21,247
(Moosquiat's new painting, "Moomoo Market")

711
00:24:21,477 --> 00:24:23,177
(I like the painting.)

712
00:24:23,817 --> 00:24:25,147
(He purchased it for 500 dollars.)

713
00:24:25,687 --> 00:24:28,017
(And Sung Hwan had his eyes on this item.)

714
00:24:28,457 --> 00:24:30,487
(The Grand Award Air when he won the award)

715
00:24:30,657 --> 00:24:32,657
(I'll pay 600 dollars for both.)

716
00:24:32,887 --> 00:24:35,727
(He donated a total of 1,000 dollars for everything.)

717
00:24:35,997 --> 00:24:39,727
At the bazaar, CODE KUNST brought the bottle.

718
00:24:39,927 --> 00:24:42,067
I'm delivering it on his behalf.

719
00:24:42,267 --> 00:24:44,466
Since he's the first client to buy my art,

720
00:24:44,467 --> 00:24:47,307
I'll tell him where to place it. I'm like a curator.

721
00:24:48,177 --> 00:24:50,136
- Come here, Hyun Moo. - Give me a tour of your house.

722
00:24:50,137 --> 00:24:52,477
Yes. But it got cold. I didn't want to waste time for you.

723
00:24:52,547 --> 00:24:54,346
So I already prepared it.

724
00:24:54,347 --> 00:24:56,247
- What? - My gosh. What's that?

725
00:24:56,777 --> 00:24:57,886
- Gnocchi? - Gnocchi.

726
00:24:57,887 --> 00:24:59,187
(Have some gnocchi.)

727
00:24:59,387 --> 00:25:01,357
- So I already prepared it. - He wanted to feed me too.

728
00:25:02,717 --> 00:25:04,056
(I already had three meals.)

729
00:25:04,057 --> 00:25:06,457
Everyone gave you food when you visited them.

730
00:25:06,927 --> 00:25:08,357
I hadn't felt this loved in a while.

731
00:25:09,597 --> 00:25:10,797
I saw it coming.

732
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:13,367
I could smell food the moment I started to walk up the stairs.

733
00:25:13,967 --> 00:25:15,897
I knew it. "He's cooking."

734
00:25:15,937 --> 00:25:18,807
But I was so full already.

735
00:25:19,107 --> 00:25:20,536
(Feeling bloated)

736
00:25:20,537 --> 00:25:22,437
- You'll be surprised by the taste. - Okay.

737
00:25:22,877 --> 00:25:24,576
(Chuckling)

738
00:25:24,577 --> 00:25:26,477
It's very tasty. Now comes something we like.

739
00:25:27,277 --> 00:25:28,946
- That's right. - It's really tasty.

740
00:25:28,947 --> 00:25:30,146
Do another round of pepper.

741
00:25:30,147 --> 00:25:31,616
I thought you wouldn't like it. I prefer it that way too.

742
00:25:31,617 --> 00:25:32,917
"I thought you wouldn't like it."

743
00:25:34,217 --> 00:25:35,217
(Full of pepper)

744
00:25:35,218 --> 00:25:36,787
- Are you serious? - Of course.

745
00:25:36,857 --> 00:25:38,356
It isn't much when you mix it in.

746
00:25:38,357 --> 00:25:39,687
(I love pepper.)

747
00:25:39,887 --> 00:25:42,157
Why are you guys having a match of pride?

748
00:25:42,497 --> 00:25:43,657
I like it much more.

749
00:25:44,367 --> 00:25:46,427
- Hyun Moo, please sit there. - Okay.

750
00:25:46,727 --> 00:25:47,797
Kkotbun.

751
00:25:48,267 --> 00:25:51,937
Hyun Moo, it's only a small amount.

752
00:25:52,237 --> 00:25:53,237
(Feeling bloated)

753
00:25:53,238 --> 00:25:55,576
I had four meals.

754
00:25:55,577 --> 00:25:56,837
(I had four meals.)

755
00:25:57,677 --> 00:25:59,246
- Stop giving me food. - Do you know what it is?

756
00:25:59,247 --> 00:26:00,277
- Olive oil. - Gosh!

757
00:26:00,877 --> 00:26:02,617
- Truffle. - Truffle oil?

758
00:26:03,377 --> 00:26:05,617
- It's expensive. - You need to add truffle oil.

759
00:26:05,947 --> 00:26:07,387
You need to add an excessive amount.

760
00:26:07,517 --> 00:26:09,457
- Do you smell it? - I smell it.

761
00:26:09,617 --> 00:26:11,357
- It looks so tasty. - Gnocchi.

762
00:26:12,627 --> 00:26:13,826
- It looks tasty. - Right?

763
00:26:13,827 --> 00:26:14,857
Yes.

764
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,266
Even if you're full, try a bite...

765
00:26:17,267 --> 00:26:18,867
- because I'll eat the rest. - I'll try it.

766
00:26:19,167 --> 00:26:20,326
- Try it. - You made it with effort.

767
00:26:20,327 --> 00:26:21,536
(I'll try it. You made it with effort.)

768
00:26:21,537 --> 00:26:22,597
It's tasty.

769
00:26:25,067 --> 00:26:26,137
Thank you for the food.

770
00:26:30,607 --> 00:26:31,777
Be honest.

771
00:26:33,347 --> 00:26:35,947
Honestly, how does it taste? How is this amateur's cooking skill?

772
00:26:37,347 --> 00:26:39,087
- It's good, right? - Listen.

773
