01:14:36,931 --> 01:14:38,201
Wait. Is it that one?

2062
01:14:39,061 --> 01:14:40,171
That must be it.

2063
01:14:40,301 --> 01:14:42,330
It's the one with a yellow sign.

2064
01:14:42,331 --> 01:14:43,441
Where? Oh, you're right.

2065
01:14:45,501 --> 01:14:46,670
No way. They found it.

2066
01:14:46,671 --> 01:14:48,440
(A block toy store with a yellow sign at the end of the arcade)

2067
01:14:48,441 --> 01:14:50,180
- It's really small. - Yes, it's very small.

2068
01:14:50,181 --> 01:14:51,210
- What is that? - It looks like...

2069
01:14:51,211 --> 01:14:52,481
an unmanned ice cream shop.

2070
01:14:53,411 --> 01:14:54,450
- For real. - I know.

2071
01:14:54,451 --> 01:14:56,420
You wouldn't notice it if you walk past it.

2072
01:14:56,421 --> 01:14:57,951
(Relatable)

2073
01:14:58,251 --> 01:15:00,821
Gosh, there are block toys inside.

2074
01:15:01,391 --> 01:15:02,391
Let's go inside.

2075
01:15:02,761 --> 01:15:04,261
Hey, be careful.

2076
01:15:04,691 --> 01:15:05,721
You're so excited.

2077
01:15:06,031 --> 01:15:07,490
Gosh, look at the inside.

2078
01:15:07,491 --> 01:15:08,890
(Today's destination they've waited the whole day for)

2079
01:15:08,891 --> 01:15:10,600
- Gosh, hello, sir. - Oh, my!

2080
01:15:10,601 --> 01:15:11,601
Gosh.

2081
01:15:13,431 --> 01:15:15,330
Gosh, the inside is the treasure trove.

2082
01:15:15,331 --> 01:15:18,101
(The treasure trove filled with block toys)

2083
01:15:19,671 --> 01:15:21,470
Gosh, a block enthusiast must've opened that store.

2084
01:15:21,471 --> 01:15:22,570
- That's right. - Right?

2085
01:15:22,571 --> 01:15:23,581
Yes.

2086
01:15:24,311 --> 01:15:27,710
(There are even unopened new products.)

2087
01:15:27,711 --> 01:15:30,421
Why did he buy them if he wasn't going to assemble them?

2088
01:15:30,621 --> 01:15:31,920
He wants to...

2089
01:15:31,921 --> 01:15:33,890
- just collect them. - That's right.

2090
01:15:33,891 --> 01:15:35,390
Even for comic books,

2091
01:15:35,391 --> 01:15:36,860
if it's the first edition of "Dragon Ball,"

2092
01:15:36,861 --> 01:15:39,191
- you'd keep them unopened. - That's right.

2093
01:15:39,331 --> 01:15:41,430
- It's like that. - Oh, that's how they think.

2094
01:15:41,431 --> 01:15:43,330
You know the drama, "Winter Sonata?"

2095
01:15:43,331 --> 01:15:44,600
Yes, one with Yon-sama.

2096
01:15:44,601 --> 01:15:46,830
The fans have one for displaying, one solely for collection,

2097
01:15:46,831 --> 01:15:47,901
and one for watching.

2098
01:15:48,431 --> 01:15:49,970
- They have 3 sets each? - They buy 3 sets.

2099
01:15:49,971 --> 01:15:52,910
Those who really love block toys buy 2 or 3 sets.

2100
01:15:52,911 --> 01:15:54,170
- That's right. - Oh, one for keeps...

2101
01:15:54,171 --> 01:15:55,310
- They don't open it at all. - and one for assembling.

2102
01:15:55,311 --> 01:15:56,841
Gosh, they'd need a big storage.

2103
01:15:58,981 --> 01:16:03,781
(The block toys fill the wide shelf.)

2104
01:16:05,681 --> 01:16:07,090
(There are even products with set numbers in three digits.)

2105
01:16:07,091 --> 01:16:08,520
- What's that? - Set numbers...

2106
01:16:08,521 --> 01:16:10,320
indicate the order of release.

2107
01:16:10,321 --> 01:16:12,690
These days, the numbers go up to something like 67,000.

2108
01:16:12,691 --> 01:16:14,560
If it's 554,

2109
01:16:14,561 --> 01:16:16,501
that means it was released in the 70s or 80s.

2110
01:16:17,231 --> 01:16:19,770
- That must be really precious. - It's expensive.

2111
01:16:19,771 --> 01:16:21,700
- It was released in the early days. - Like really long ago.

2112
01:16:21,701 --> 01:16:23,341
That's the vintage product.

2113
01:16:23,401 --> 01:16:24,771
It's a really old vintage product.

2114
01:16:25,271 --> 01:16:26,710
My mother bought me one on the Children's Day...

2115
01:16:26,711 --> 01:16:28,140
when I was in elementary school.

2116
01:16:28,141 --> 01:16:31,281
It was an underwater exploration set called the Aqua Set.

2117
01:16:31,781 --> 01:16:33,851
It was a little over 100 dollars.

2118
01:16:33,981 --> 01:16:35,611
But now, it costs around 2,000 to 3,000 dollars.

2119
01:16:37,321 --> 01:16:39,621
The brand has a long history.

2120
01:16:41,221 --> 01:16:43,691
- This is crazy. - The block toys I've never seen.

2121
01:16:43,921 --> 01:16:46,091
These days,

2122
01:16:46,261 --> 01:16:47,830
I'm even studying block toy products.

2123
01:16:47,831 --> 01:16:49,130
- You're even studying them? - Yes.

2124
01:16:49,131 --> 01:16:51,901
Like which set has which characteristics.

2125
01:16:51,931 --> 01:16:53,301
You're studying them. I see.

2126
01:16:53,631 --> 01:16:54,700
Gosh, seriously...

2127
01:16:54,701 --> 01:16:55,701
(Going forward as though he's possessed)

2128
01:16:55,702 --> 01:16:58,001
(Amazed)

2129
01:16:58,141 --> 01:17:00,340
So these are the old block toy sets.

2130
01:17:00,341 --> 01:17:02,370
- You're right. - If you look here,

2131
01:17:02,371 --> 01:17:04,740
there are block toy sets released in the 70s and 80s.

2132
01:17:04,741 --> 01:17:06,410
The ones that say LEGOLAND.

2133
01:17:06,411 --> 01:17:07,611
That's even before I was born.

2134
01:17:09,451 --> 01:17:11,420
(The block toys started to sell in Korea in the 80s.)

2135
01:17:11,421 --> 01:17:13,120
Doesn't that make you excited?

2136
01:17:13,121 --> 01:17:14,451
(The block toys started to sell in Korea in the 80s.)

2137
01:17:16,861 --> 01:17:18,290
(Exclaiming)

2138
01:17:18,291 --> 01:17:19,791
- I think I've seen it. - Right?

2139
01:17:19,861 --> 01:17:22,190
It brings back childhood nostalgia for everyone.

2140
01:17:22,191 --> 01:17:23,260
You're right.

2141
01:17:23,261 --> 01:17:24,561
Look. It's riding a horse.

2142
01:17:25,431 --> 01:17:28,031
The System sets are from the 90s.

2143
01:17:28,171 --> 01:17:30,470
These were released after the 2000s.

2144
01:17:30,471 --> 01:17:31,670
There's one from another country too.

2145
01:17:31,671 --> 01:17:33,311
(The products we're more familiar with)

2146
01:17:35,141 --> 01:17:36,680
Oh, my. I remember that.

2147
01:17:36,681 --> 01:17:38,440
- I remember! - The glow-in-the-dark ghost.

2148
01:17:38,441 --> 01:17:39,651
That's right!

2149
01:17:41,751 --> 01:17:45,080
I have a strong nostalgia...

2150
01:17:45,081 --> 01:17:47,291
for old block toys.

2151
01:17:47,521 --> 01:17:49,291
The ones I liked...

2152
01:17:49,721 --> 01:17:53,191
were monkey, octopus, and shark.

2153
01:17:53,261 --> 01:17:55,431
I have a great memory of those parts.

2154
01:17:55,861 --> 01:17:57,630
Those pieces were only released at that time,

2155
01:17:57,631 --> 01:17:58,831
and they're not released anymore.

2156
01:17:59,601 --> 01:18:03,141
But I heard this store had it, so I went all the way to Busan.

2157
01:18:03,671 --> 01:18:05,400
You can travel back in time with that piece alone.

2158
01:18:05,401 --> 01:18:06,410
- That's right. - Totally.

2159
01:18:06,411 --> 01:18:08,340
I bit mine a lot, so it has a lot of teeth marks.

2160
01:18:08,341 --> 01:18:10,580
Right! You bite it off because you assembled it wrong.

2161
01:18:10,581 --> 01:18:11,910
- I see. Like this? - To take the head off.

2162
01:18:11,911 --> 01:18:13,281
And one side would be gone.

2163
01:18:14,851 --> 01:18:15,981
On your left...

2164
01:18:16,551 --> 01:18:19,081
are bikes and Batman products.

2165
01:18:20,021 --> 01:18:22,521
We even have "Harry Potter" sets.

2166
01:18:22,861 --> 01:18:25,221
- We have The Wild West sets too. - They're the old style.

2167
01:18:25,591 --> 01:18:27,291
- Gold. - Gosh.

2168
01:18:28,461 --> 01:18:29,530
Actually...

2169
01:18:29,531 --> 01:18:33,100
So these are the displayed builds.

2170
01:18:33,101 --> 01:18:35,771
- I'm into castles these days. - Castles.

2171
01:18:36,131 --> 01:18:38,570
- They're legit castles. - I'm deep in love with them.

2172
01:18:38,571 --> 01:18:40,470
- Castles? - There are castle bases...

2173
01:18:40,471 --> 01:18:42,980
and marine bases on display.

2174
01:18:42,981 --> 01:18:44,311
Gosh, they're so cool.

2175
01:18:44,441 --> 01:18:45,641
Oh, there are soldiers.

2176
01:18:47,281 --> 01:18:48,680
Even the trees are different.

2177
01:18:48,681 --> 01:18:50,780
- They're old trees. Cypress trees. - I know. They're old trees.

2178
01:18:50,781 --> 01:18:52,920
I can tell at a glance. Such trees aren't released these days.

2179
01:18:52,921 --> 01:18:54,220
Every the block toy tree looked like that.

2180
01:18:54,221 --> 01:18:55,350
I know.

2181
01:18:55,351 --> 01:18:57,461
That tree is really expensive now.

2182
01:18:57,661 --> 01:18:59,690
Because they're not released anymore.

2183
01:18:59,691 --> 01:19:01,130
So some sell only the trees.

2184
01:19:01,131 --> 01:19:02,760
- Those trees aren't sold anymore. - Yes.

2185
01:19:02,761 --> 01:19:04,400
They used to be everywhere, rolling around on the floor,

2186
01:19:04,401 --> 01:19:06,030
at our friends' places.

2187
01:19:06,031 --> 01:19:07,970
They'd be under the sofa as well.

2188
01:19:07,971 --> 01:19:09,570
- We'd run around and step on them, - Right, when we step on them,

2189
01:19:09,571 --> 01:19:11,000
- and we'd scream. - it'd hurt badly.

2190
01:19:11,001 --> 01:19:12,910
- We'd bump our little toes into it. - Right.

2191
01:19:12,911 --> 01:19:13,940
We'd see it everywhere.

2192
01:19:13,941 --> 01:19:15,470
- And that's expensive now? - Yes.

2193
01:19:15,471 --> 01:19:17,541
It's crazy because people want to get the tree only.

2194
01:19:17,711 --> 01:19:18,880
I should've collected them from then.

2195
01:19:18,881 --> 01:19:20,610
- That's exactly what I'm saying. - Seriously.

2196
01:19:20,611 --> 01:19:22,250
- I should've collected the trees. - Seriously. They were just...

2197
01:19:22,251 --> 01:19:23,520
(If we just collected the trees under the sofa...)

2198
01:19:23,521 --> 01:19:24,920
Is this the Knights' Castle?

2199
01:19:24,921 --> 01:19:26,720
- Yes, it's Lion Knights' Castle. - Right. Lion Knights' Castle.

2200
01:19:26,721 --> 01:19:28,791
- It was recently discontinued. - That's right.

2201
01:19:28,851 --> 01:19:30,990
They said I should buy it...

2202
01:19:30,991 --> 01:19:32,760
before the price rises even if it's secondhand.

2203
01:19:32,761 --> 01:19:34,031
- You mean Lion Knights' Castle? - Yes.

2204
01:19:34,091 --> 01:19:35,761
- This one's cool. - It's cool, right?

2205
01:19:36,301 --> 01:19:38,731
This one's really cool.

2206
01:19:40,101 --> 01:19:41,900
- Yes, it's chrome. - That's crazy.

2207
01:19:41,901 --> 01:19:43,541
It's chrome.

2208
01:19:43,601 --> 01:19:44,900
(A chrome knight)

2209
01:19:44,901 --> 01:19:46,270
This one is really cool.

2210
01:19:46,271 --> 01:19:48,510
I assembled this yesterday.

2211
01:19:48,511 --> 01:19:49,880
Oh, really? Yesterday?

2212
01:19:49,881 --> 01:19:51,140
- The owner is excited. - The owner is excited.

2213
01:19:51,141 --> 01:19:52,211
(Curious)

2214
01:19:52,281 --> 01:19:53,311
It's a shark.

2215
01:19:53,411 --> 01:19:55,081
- A shark. - There's a shark.

2216
01:19:55,681 --> 01:19:58,051
This is the headquarters of a pirate base.

2217
01:19:58,421 --> 01:20:00,321
It's also from the 90s.

2218
01:20:00,421 --> 01:20:02,391
I'm getting goosebumps.

2219
01:20:03,161 --> 01:20:07,191
Because I love block toys so much,

2220
01:20:07,491 --> 01:20:11,401
I jump from time to time even when we're talking about it.

2221
01:20:11,661 --> 01:20:14,530
Like how we're gathered here. It's just a toy, actually.

2222
01:20:14,531 --> 01:20:16,541
We'd gather like this and talk about a toy.

2223
01:20:16,901 --> 01:20:18,840
We're like, "This is the marine base."

2224
01:20:18,841 --> 01:20:20,071
(Serious)

2225
01:20:20,141 --> 01:20:21,910
- This is... - I also thought that way.

2226
01:20:21,911 --> 01:20:24,180
- It is indeed awkward. - I also...

2227
01:20:24,181 --> 01:20:26,681
Three fully grown men would look at the plastic toy and go,

2228
01:20:26,751 --> 01:20:28,480
- "This is the marine base." - "This is the marine base."

2229
01:20:28,481 --> 01:20:30,051
- "This is..." - It's from the 90s.

2230
01:20:30,151 --> 01:20:31,551
He said that's the marine base.

2231
01:20:31,751 --> 01:20:33,290
You were so funny just now.

2232
01:20:33,291 --> 01:20:34,751
"There's a shark."

2233
01:20:35,251 --> 01:20:36,321
You said it as if...

2234
01:20:36,921 --> 01:20:40,291
(I can't take it easy when it comes to sharks.)

2235
01:20:42,861 --> 01:20:44,161
Please be careful.

2236
01:20:44,331 --> 01:20:45,700
- What is it? - Let me through.

2237
01:20:45,701 --> 01:20:48,070
I don't think he was telling me to be careful.

2238
01:20:48,071 --> 01:20:49,100
Oh, right.

2239
01:20:49,101 --> 01:20:50,471
Oh, be careful of the toys?

2240
01:20:52,441 --> 01:20:53,970
(How careful must we be?)

2241
01:20:53,971 --> 01:20:55,311
If you look inside...

2242
01:20:57,141 --> 01:20:58,210
(The space where there's a door lock)

2243
01:20:58,211 --> 01:20:59,650
Gosh, it's double protected.

2244
01:20:59,651 --> 01:21:01,251
There was a door lock on it too.

2245
01:21:02,051 --> 01:21:05,281
(In the corner of the block toy store...)

2246
01:21:08,151 --> 01:21:09,861
There are only rare products in there.

2247
01:21:10,321 --> 01:21:11,321
Really?

2248
01:21:11,322 --> 01:21:12,691
There are only truly rare products.

2249
01:21:14,631 --> 01:21:16,861
(A splendid lineup)

2250
01:21:19,161 --> 01:21:21,970
I'm sure there are a few that'd make you nostalgic.

2251
01:21:21,971 --> 01:21:23,001
(Filled with vintage block toys)

2252
01:21:23,741 --> 01:21:24,900
This is the most expensive one...

2253
01:21:24,901 --> 01:21:26,070
- in my store. - Really?

2254
01:21:26,071 --> 01:21:28,271
- It's 6,000 dollars. - This is 6,000 dollars?

2255
01:21:28,671 --> 01:21:29,680
What, 6,000 dollars?

2256
01:21:29,681 --> 01:21:31,111
- It's 6,000 dollars? - He said that's 6,000 dollars.

2257
01:21:31,181 --> 01:21:32,740
Gosh. This is...

2258
01:21:32,741 --> 01:21:34,111
It must have a long history.

2259
01:21:34,181 --> 01:21:35,680
- It does. - How so?

2260
01:21:35,681 --> 01:21:37,481
It's the Maersk Truck from the early days.

2261
01:21:38,121 --> 01:21:39,220
It's a vintage car.

2262
01:21:39,221 --> 01:21:40,951
That's right. It's rare.

2263
01:21:41,191 --> 01:21:43,390
Cars like that aren't released anymore.

2264
01:21:43,391 --> 01:21:44,520
There must be only a few of those...

2265
01:21:44,521 --> 01:21:45,660
- around the world. - There's only a few.

2266
01:21:45,661 --> 01:21:48,861
Its value has increased a lot now.

2267
01:21:49,361 --> 01:21:51,631
- That's crazy. - Six thousand dollars?

2268
01:21:51,901 --> 01:21:54,800
- Gosh. - This is the ultimate one.

2269
01:21:54,801 --> 01:21:57,540
- It's the ultimate one? - It's the third generation.

2270
01:21:57,541 --> 01:21:59,070
It's the pirate base.

2271
01:21:59,071 --> 01:22:00,641
That was popular in our days.

2272
01:22:00,741 --> 01:22:02,140
That's right. The block toys from our days...

2273
01:22:02,141 --> 01:22:03,610
- were all about pirates. - The flag.

2274
01:22:03,611 --> 01:22:04,611
I remember.

2275
01:22:04,681 --> 01:22:06,240
This is a bat castle.

2276
01:22:06,241 --> 01:22:07,510
- Park Ji Sung? - Yes.

2277
01:22:07,511 --> 01:22:09,551
A bat castle.

2278
01:22:09,651 --> 01:22:11,050
- Oh, I see. - Yes.

2279
01:22:11,051 --> 01:22:12,120
A bat castle.

2280
01:22:12,121 --> 01:22:14,020
I thought it was a 2002-edition.

2281
01:22:14,021 --> 01:22:15,791
It was really popular in Korea too.

2282
01:22:16,821 --> 01:22:17,860
This one here.

2283
01:22:17,861 --> 01:22:19,660
Can I go inside for a second?

2284
01:22:19,661 --> 01:22:20,761
Sure. Got it.

2285
01:22:22,291 --> 01:22:24,260
(He was close to the secret room,)

2286
01:22:24,261 --> 01:22:26,201
(but he could only watch over their shoulders.)

2287
01:22:26,671 --> 01:22:27,730
- Sung Woo. - Yes?

2288
01:22:27,731 --> 01:22:29,131
One second. Let me see them too.

2289
01:22:29,401 --> 01:22:30,840
Let me see them too.

2290
01:22:30,841 --> 01:22:32,001
Hold on. Let me...

2291
01:22:33,641 --> 01:22:34,670
Gosh.

2292
01:22:34,671 --> 01:22:35,740
(Walking in)

2293
01:22:35,741 --> 01:22:36,780
(Struggling)

2294
01:22:36,781 --> 01:22:38,711
- Be careful of that at the back. - I should really be careful.

2295
01:22:40,251 --> 01:22:41,811
- Hey. - Be careful.

2296
01:22:42,781 --> 01:22:43,881
It's really...

2297
01:22:44,021 --> 01:22:45,981
(It almost fell.)

2298
01:22:47,021 --> 01:22:49,921
I'll just creep close to the ground.

2299
01:22:50,261 --> 01:22:51,560
- There are some on the bottom too. - Yes.

2300
01:22:51,561 --> 01:22:52,991
Gosh, Dong Hwi.

2301
01:22:53,531 --> 01:22:54,560
It's because of his jacket.

2302
01:22:54,561 --> 01:22:56,061
Oh, it's because of his jacket.

2303
01:22:56,561 --> 01:22:58,430
(Shaking)

2304
01:22:58,431 --> 01:22:59,871
- Be careful. It's okay. - Yes.

2305
01:23:01,631 --> 01:23:03,570
What do you mean by, "Be careful. It's okay?"

2306
01:23:03,571 --> 01:23:05,000
(What does he actually mean?)

2307
01:23:05,001 --> 01:23:06,440
- What am I supposed to do? - I...

2308
01:23:06,441 --> 01:23:08,511
(Be careful.)

2309
01:23:09,011 --> 01:23:10,540
- This is another one. - It's the glow-in-the-dark ghost.

2310
01:23:10,541 --> 01:23:11,980
It's a castle battle set.

2311
01:23:11,981 --> 01:23:13,781
I didn't expect to see the glow-in-the-dark ghost here.

2312
01:23:14,211 --> 01:23:16,010
- A shark. - There's a shark here too.

2313
01:23:16,011 --> 01:23:17,051
There's a shark here!

